       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Amlodipine 100 mg daily has no therapeutic use, and the risk to the patient is high. The maximum labeled dose is 10 mg, and the drug's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours means 100 mg doses would accumulate. For a 70 kg adult with normal organ function, I can't find a clinical scenario that justifies it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, or any dose up to 10 mg that you choose.\n- **Enter the 100 mg order** only if you can give a specific clinical rationale, such as a protocol or a toxicology or cardiology recommendation. I would put that rationale in the order note and flag it for pharmacist review.\n- **Ask pharmacy to review it with you** if you think the dose is right but aren't sure.\n\nIf you meant a different dose or a different drug, tell me and I'll enter it."
      }
